course: dictionary
lesson: 2348
title: Crying: feelings in words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Crying» usually means tears are coming from your eyes, often because you are sad, hurt or scared. Picture coming second in a race and crying, even though second is brilliant. The tears show strong feelings, and the words around them give the clue: second is good, but the feelings are still big.
explain: Crying can also mean shouting loudly, as in «crying for help» or «crying out». In that case there may be no tears at all. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? If shouting still makes sense when you swap it in, you have the right meaning.
explain: In Edinburgh, Olivia hears her mam greetin' at night since Granny died. Greetin' is Scots for crying. The clue is Granny died, so this is sad crying, not happy crying. Clues in the context tell you the feeling.
fact: «Crying» means having tears coming from your eyes, usually because you are sad, hurt or scared.
fact: People also cry when they are very happy or laughing hard.
fact: «Crying for help» or «crying out» means shouting loudly.
fact: Phrases to know: «burst out crying», «cry your eyes out», «stop crying».
fact: Spelling: cry becomes cried, but crying keeps the y, so it is spelled crying, not criing.
exercise: «Picture coming second in a race and crying, even though second is brilliant.» What do the tears most likely show? | Hunger at lunchtime | Tiredness after a long run | Nothing at all, the tears are just water | *Strong feelings, even though second place is good
exercise: In Dundee, Callie's mam says, «Ye're fine, stop greetin'». What does greetin' mean? | Shouting for help | *Crying | Eating a snack | Greeting her friends at the door
exercise: Which sentence uses crying to mean shouting loudly? | *«He was crying out for help in the snow.» | «Crying is a healthy thing to do.» | «The baby was crying in her cot.» | «She burst out crying at the film.»
test: Why might a baby be crying? Babies cannot speak. | *Because they are hungry, tired or uncomfortable | Because they want to go to school | Because they have won a race | Because they are reading a book
test: Which is the correct spelling of the -ing form of cry? | criing | *crying | cryng | cring
exam: Which statement about crying is true? | Crying is always a sign of being unwell | *Anyone, boys or girls, children or adults, may cry | Crying is only for people who are badly hurt | Only babies cry
